      "content": "I see. Following that logic of 'eroding identity,' do you think there's a distinction in how this'loss of familiarness' is experienced depending on the specific immigrant groups involved? For instance, when looking at certain groups that have higher rates of clustering or different social organization models, does that tend to accelerate the perception of a decline in social cohesion compared to more integrated groups? I'm trying to figure out if certain demographics are inherently more 'challenging' to the existing social fabric based on these sociological patterns.",
